; fs: filesystems on the drop-in (unit 5, after pre: it wrote that unit).
; Mounts SBA: (FFS2) and SBB: (SFS) from sb.mountlist, formats both, copies
; SYS:C and SYS:Libs to each and hashes the copies. Then start fs-par A and
; fs-par B as two jobs at once (two Shells), then reboot and run fs-remount.
;   Execute SHARED:sbench/fs
FailAt 30
MakeDir SHARED:sbench/out >NIL:
Mount SBA: FROM SHARED:sbench/sb.mountlist
Mount SBB: FROM SHARED:sbench/sb.mountlist
Echo "" >RAM:cr
SYS:System/Format <RAM:cr DRIVE SBA: NAME SBFFS QUICK NOICONS
SYS:System/Format <RAM:cr DRIVE SBB: NAME SBSFS QUICK NOICONS
CD SYS:
C:MD5Sum C/#? Libs/#? >SHARED:sbench/out/fs-src.md5
CD RAM:
Copy SYS:C SBA:C ALL QUIET
Copy SYS:Libs SBA:Libs ALL QUIET
Copy SYS:C SBB:C ALL QUIET
Copy SYS:Libs SBB:Libs ALL QUIET
CD SBA:
C:MD5Sum C/#? Libs/#? >SHARED:sbench/out/fs-ffs.md5
CD SBB:
C:MD5Sum C/#? Libs/#? >SHARED:sbench/out/fs-sfs.md5
CD RAM:
Info SBA:
Info SBB:
Echo "fs done" >SHARED:sbench/out/fs.done
